WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.273
Welcome to Master 01 for EXL Salesforce COE Resource 360.

2
00:00:05.273 --> 00:00:20.565
This live Salesforce walkthrough covers six distinct global experiences: identity assurance, the role-aware home, actionable notifications, governed cross-object search, role and scope selection, and personal preferences with contextual guidance.

3
00:00:20.565 --> 00:00:30.056
Every transition is selected in the product, and every action produces a visible result using fictional demo data.

4
00:00:31.256 --> 00:00:34.027
GLB-01 proves the authenticated entry contract.

5
00:00:34.027 --> 00:00:41.415
We select Verify session, and Salesforce resolves the current identity, assigned permission groups and authorized scope.

6
00:00:41.415 --> 00:00:47.879
The successful verification outcome appears on the screen before Continue opens the role-aware home.

7
00:00:47.879 --> 00:00:56.652
In production, EXL identity federation would replace the developer-org login; the server-side authorization and audit contract remains the same.

8
00:00:57.852 --> 00:01:01.955
GLB-02 is an operational home rather than a generic menu.

9
00:01:01.955 --> 00:01:06.469
Capacity, commercial and delivery signals come from the seeded Salesforce records.

10
00:01:06.469 --> 00:01:15.497
We choose the Delivery priority, which opens the scoped engagement portfolio, then return through the visible module control and continue to notifications.

11
00:01:15.497 --> 00:01:20.422
The destination changes with the active persona while record security remains authoritative.

12
00:01:21.622 --> 00:01:25.040
GLB-03 turns alerts into an accountable exception queue.

13
00:01:25.040 --> 00:01:30.595
We filter for high severity, select a specific notification and mark it reviewed.

14
00:01:30.595 --> 00:01:35.296
The selected state exposes category, owner, business context and review evidence.

15
00:01:35.296 --> 00:01:44.697
A notification can lead only to records already authorized for the user, so the inbox cannot bypass portfolio sharing or commercial confidentiality.

16
00:01:47.622 --> 00:01:51.258
GLB-04 provides governed discovery across Resource 360 objects.

17
00:01:51.258 --> 00:02:00.350
We search for Architect, filter the result set to practitioners, select a named result and open its Resource 360 drill-down.

18
00:02:00.350 --> 00:02:07.169
The result explains object type and context, while user-mode queries and scope controls determine visibility.

19
00:02:07.169 --> 00:02:10.351
Empty, filtered and unauthorized outcomes remain distinguishable.

20
00:02:14.422 --> 00:02:17.392
GLB-05 makes the active operating context explicit.

21
00:02:17.392 --> 00:02:22.485
We select Project Manager, choose an authorized portfolio scope and apply it.

22
00:02:22.485 --> 00:02:26.304
The visible outcome confirms the effective persona and boundary.

23
00:02:26.304 --> 00:02:36.489
This interaction never grants authority by itself: Salesforce permission sets, sharing, delegation dates and user-mode enforcement still decide which records and actions are available.

24
00:02:40.822 --> 00:02:44.114
GLB-06 combines personal preferences with task-specific guidance.

25
00:02:44.114 --> 00:02:51.168
We change display density and time zone, save the settings, then launch the engagement guide.

26
00:02:51.168 --> 00:02:57.282
The action opens the relevant Salesforce journey instead of returning a generic response.

27
00:02:57.282 --> 00:03:05.748
This completes the global foundation: verified identity, purposeful home, actionable exceptions, governed search, explicit context and reusable help.
